      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "ROCK THE MIC (3) brings the most persuasive recent form after consecutive seconds, the latest in a BM54+ at Belmont Park when beaten just over three lengths by Capable Angel after coming from a long way back and being bumped at the start. Dropping from that grade into a Mdn gives him the right profile to break through. SAISOKU (2) is the clear danger on consistency, with placings at Bunbury and this track and a solid record of six minor placings from twelve starts. He has also placed on wet ground, which is useful with the surface in the soft range. YALDA NIGHT (1) is harder to trust for the win after a market-cold fifth at Belmont Park, but his track-and-distance record keeps him in the place mix. TAGOLORIAN (6) was beaten six lengths behind Mystacheeno at this venue and has been unwanted in betting, so he has to find more, though he is fitter third-up and remains lightly raced enough to hold minor claims. ROCK SILVER (4) can improve out in trip.",
